# Governance surface — requires James's review, never auto-merged.
#
# This file is what bounds the I6a merge grant. arbi and Guilfoyle may merge their own
# PRs once required checks pass (docs/product/arbi-permission-model.md), which would
# otherwise let the agent merge a change to its own charter, permission ladder, or
# guard hooks. Everything below is excluded from that grant: a PR touching these paths
# blocks on review regardless of CI status.
#
# Requires "Require review from Code Owners" to be enabled in branch protection on
# main. Without that setting this file is advisory only.

# The agent's own authority, boundaries, and scorecard.
#
# Listed file-by-file rather than as /docs/product/ wholesale. That directory holds two
# different kinds of file: BOUNDARY files that define what arbi may do, and MEMORY files
# (roadmap-state, decision-log, run-ledger, inbox, handoffs) that arbi must write on every
# wake and close. Gating the memory files would put a human in the loop of every routine
# /arbi-close, which is friction that gets routed around rather than complied with — and
# the merge is already gated by CI. Only the boundaries need James's eyes.
/docs/product/north-star.md            @Jp8617465-sys
/docs/product/arbi-constitution.md     @Jp8617465-sys
/docs/product/arbi-permission-model.md @Jp8617465-sys
/docs/product/arbi-authority.md        @Jp8617465-sys
/docs/product/arbi-scorecard.md        @Jp8617465-sys

